A||||2||fieroc4||Autocross was suspension options||||5||
Z||000000||fieroc4||02-03-2000||03:51 AM||||&gt;&gt;Someone may find out what your car is riding on and take you out of Cstock.&lt;&lt;<P>Does this make any difference?  I'm thinking about trying SOLO II just for fun, and to improve MY skills.  Probably the Fiero is better stock than I am and I'd be out classed in both driving skill and car prep for modified classes, but won't I still have FUN?<P>I've always wanted a first class handling car that looked good, so bye-bye 14" rims hello 15"s (and looking for 17's), I'm out of stock class.  Lower it using drop spindles, or koni coil-overs, maybe both.  Not to mention the other suspenion mods around.  I want more power, this is my street car, so larger valves, higher compression and header.  Now I'm way out of stock class.<P>From my understanding what I've just described would only be allowed to compete with purpose built race cars, I'd get smoked.  The 17's aren't allowed 16x10 are the largest from what I've read, so I guess I could get some really sticky 15" tires and use the 15" rims I already have just swap at the course.<P>A couple of years ago I talked to a local offical and he told me that no one would say anything about my 15" rims until I started winning then I'd probably have to get stock rims or switch classes.  Right now that's the only mod I've done, but I'm getting more time and money to spend on my ride.<P>What options do I have with what I'd like and what the rules allow?  Or can I not worry about what class I end up in and just LEARN car control and have FUN?<P>Dan||||reg||5
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||02-03-2000||09:16 AM||||<BR>I agree 100%.  I build my cars for me, not for some class that have a thousand rules that change every year.  Sure, there are people who are serious about winning or doing the best they can in their class, but I take the approach that whatever I end up with after my choice of mods, then fit the car in a particular class. <P>One example of this is with my Mustang, its built my way, and because of the blower, was stuck in E Mod class with my nearly stock suspension.  Of course I ended up last at the end of the day, but I had 'Fun' with a capital F.  <P>Another example to think about are some of my friends who try and compete competively (in drag racing tho).  They spend thousands and thousands of dollars changing their combos becuase the rules change every year, and they *****  to no end about how this 'consumes' their lives and money.  Most of the time, it doesn't look like they are having fun.  <P>I've rambled on enough........<P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/</A> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Eric||02-03-2000||02:51 PM||||Hey man, don't sweat it.  It's true the rules don't allow for much, but don't let that stop you.  I recently completed a 3.1 rebuild to my 88GT and you better believe I'm not going to tell any of the tech inspectors that.  I don't even think I'd be allowed in Cstreet prepared if I divulged that.  When I competed last year, I had wider than stock tires on my stock wheels (they gave me trouble over my wheels because, in their opinion, "They don't look stock." they never noticed the tires)  I also had a shortened shifter and a few other somewhat obvious goodies.  The point is keep your mouth shut.  Don't go bragging about what mods you've done and no body will say anything.  Bending the rules is part of racing and if you don't believe me just ask ANYONE associated with professional racing.<P>15 inch wheels will keep you out of trouble as long as they are Fiero wheels.  Whose going to give you trouble about having Fiero wheels on a Fiero?<P>If you want bragging rights, use street tires.  You will get credit for not using race tires and you can run your mouth about beating some Miata that has slicks on it.<P>It's all about having fun, unfortunatly some guys take it really seriously and can be a pain in your butt.  I just like drifting through corners knocking down cones.  It's a good time!<P>Hey do a 3.4 buildup with stock manifolds and everything and get a really big cam with that idles like a dragster.  When they hear that thing fire up, they'll be like "What's in that car?  You got a cam it that or something?"  Then you can say "I don't know?  Maybe you guys should tear it down and find out."  You know just to mess with them.||||reg||6
